---

### HIGH Severity

#### 1. Conditional Test Logic
**Ref:** Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020 — *Conditional Test Logic*
**Test:** `ProcessOrder_SetsCorrectStatus` (line 24)

```csharp
if (result.TotalAmount > 100)
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
else
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
```

**Risk:** One branch never executes — you don't know which status is actually being verified. A bug could hide in the untested path.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_UnderThreshold_SetsStandardStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_OverThreshold_SetsPremiumStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-EXPENSIVE", 5) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

---

#### 2. Assertion-Free Test (a.k.a. Unknown Test / Empty Test)
**Ref:** Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020 — *Unknown Test*
**Test:** `ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError` (line 43)

```csharp
processor.ProcessOrder(order);
// ← no assertion
```

**Risk:** This test passes even if the method returns garbage. It provides false confidence — coverage goes up, defect detection stays at zero.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_SingleItem_ReturnsProcessedResult()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    var result = processor.ProcessOrder(order);

    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

---

#### 3. Mystery Guest
**Ref:** van Deursen et al., 2001 — *Mystery Guest*
**Test:** `ImportOrders_FromCsv_ParsesCorrectly` (line 140)

```csharp
File.ReadAllText(@"C:\TestData\orders.csv")
```

**Risk:** Hard-coded absolute path to an external file. Test will fail on any machine that doesn't have `C:\TestData\orders.csv`, in any CI environment, and on any non-Windows OS.

**Fix — inline the test data:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ImportOrders_FromCsv_ParsesCorrectly()
